{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IteratorProtocol","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorProtocol\/Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:St7ElementQa","text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"code":"IteratorProtocol","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol is tightly linked with the "},{"code":"Sequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"protocol. Sequences provide access to their elements by creating an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"iterator, which keeps track of its iteration process and returns one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"element at a time as it advances through the sequence."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whenever you use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop with an array, set, or any other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collection or sequence, you’re using that type’s iterator. Swift uses a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence’s or collection’s iterator internally to enable the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"loop language construct."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using a sequence’s iterator directly gives you access to the same elements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the same order as iterating over that sequence using a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"For example, you might typically use a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop to print each of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the elements in an array."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let animals = [\"Antelope\", \"Butterfly\", \"Camel\", \"Dolphin\"]","for animal in animals {","    print(animal)","}","\/\/ Prints \"Antelope\"","\/\/ Prints \"Butterfly\"","\/\/ Prints \"Camel\"","\/\/ Prints \"Dolphin\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Behind the scenes, Swift uses the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"animals"},{"type":"text","text":" array’s iterator to loop over"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the contents of the array."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["var animalIterator = animals.makeIterator()","while let animal = animalIterator.next() {","    print(animal)","}","\/\/ Prints \"Antelope\"","\/\/ Prints \"Butterfly\"","\/\/ Prints \"Camel\"","\/\/ Prints \"Dolphin\""],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The call to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"animals.makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" returns an instance of the array’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator. Next, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"while"},{"type":"text","text":" loop calls the iterator’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"repeatedly, binding each element that is returned to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"animal"},{"type":"text","text":" and exiting"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" method returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":1,"text":"Using Iterators Directly","anchor":"Using-Iterators-Directly","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You rarely need to use iterators directly, because a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loop is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more idiomatic approach to traversing a sequence in Swift. Some"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms, however, may call for direct iterator use."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"One example is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce1(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. Similar to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method defined in the standard library, which takes an initial value and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"combining closure, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce1(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses the first element of the sequence as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the initial value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Here’s an implementation of the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce1(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The sequence’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iterator is used directly to retrieve the initial value before looping"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"over the rest of the sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["extension Sequence {","    func reduce1(","        _ nextPartialResult: (Element, Element) -> Element","    ) -> Element?","    {","        var i = makeIterator()","        guard var accumulated = i.next() else {","            return nil","        }","","        while let element = i.next() {","            accumulated = nextPartialResult(accumulated, element)","        }","        return accumulated","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce1(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method makes certain kinds of sequence operations"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"simpler. Here’s how to find the longest string in a sequence, using the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"animals"},{"type":"text","text":" array introduced earlier as an example:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let longestAnimal = animals.reduce1 { current, element in","    if current.count > element.count {","        return current","    } else {","        return element","    }","}","print(longestAnimal)","\/\/ Prints Optional(\"Butterfly\")"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":1,"text":"Using Multiple Iterators","anchor":"Using-Multiple-Iterators","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Whenever you use multiple iterators (or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loops) over a single"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence, be sure you know that the specific sequence supports repeated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"iteration, either because you know its concrete type or because the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sequence is also constrained to the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Collection"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Obtain each separate iterator from separate calls to the sequence’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" method rather than by copying. Copying an iterator is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"safe, but advancing one copy of an iterator by calling its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may invalidate other copies of that iterator. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"type":"text","text":"-"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"in"},{"type":"text","text":" loops are safe in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this regard."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":1,"text":"Adding IteratorProtocol Conformance to Your Type","anchor":"Adding-IteratorProtocol-Conformance-to-Your-Type","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Implementing an iterator that conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IteratorProtocol"},{"type":"text","text":" is simple."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Declare a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" method that advances one step in the related sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and returns the current element. When the sequence has been exhausted, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" method returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For example, consider a custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Countdown"},{"type":"text","text":" sequence. You can initialize the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Countdown"},{"type":"text","text":" sequence with a starting integer and then iterate over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"count down to zero. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Countdown"},{"type":"text","text":" structure’s definition is short: It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"contains only the starting count and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" method required"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"},{"type":"text","text":" protocol."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct Countdown: Sequence {","    let start: Int","","    func makeIterator() -> CountdownIterator {","        return CountdownIterator(self)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"makeIterator()"},{"type":"text","text":" method returns another custom type, an iterator named"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CountdownIterator"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CountdownIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" type keeps track of both the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Countdown"},{"type":"text","text":" sequence that it’s iterating and the number of times it has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned a value."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct CountdownIterator: IteratorProtocol {","    let countdown: Countdown","    var times = 0","","    init(_ countdown: Countdown) {","        self.countdown = countdown","    }","","    mutating func next() -> Int? {","        let nextNumber = countdown.start - times","        guard nextNumber > 0","            else { return nil }","","        times += 1","        return nextNumber","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each time the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"next()"},{"type":"text","text":" method is called on a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CountdownIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" instance,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it calculates the new next value, checks to see whether it has reached"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"zero, and then returns either the number, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" if the iterator is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"finished returning elements of the sequence."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Creating and iterating over a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Countdown"},{"type":"text","text":" sequence uses a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CountdownIterator"},{"type":"text","text":" to handle the iteration."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let threeTwoOne = Countdown(start: 3)","for count in threeTwoOne {","    print(\"\\(count)...\")","}","\/\/ Prints \"3...\"","\/\/ Prints \"2...\"","\/\/ Prints \"1...\""],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorProtocol\/Element"],"title":"Associated Types","anchor":"Associated-Types","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Swift\/IteratorProtocol\/next()"],"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","generated":true}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"IteratorProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"Swift"}],"platforms":[{"name":"iOS","introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"iPadOS","introducedAt":"8.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"Mac Catalyst","introducedAt":"13.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"macOS","introducedAt":"10.10","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"name":"tvOS","introducedAt":"9.0","deprecated":false,"unavailable":false,"beta":false},{"unavailable":false,"name":"visionOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0"},{"unavailable":false,"name":"watchOS","deprecated":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"2.0"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","title":"IteratorProtocol","externalID":"s:St","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"IteratorProtocol","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swift\/iteratorprotocol"]}]